Hi [~accountid:61d554bb68926d00685d5727] - getting back to you with further responses:

----

{quote}_In terms of tactical design, what categories would these consents come to?_{quote}

All identified use cases fall under *analytical* and/or *targeting* categories, both of which require user consent. These categories can be adjusted if needed when designing the consent interface.

{quote}_If we do not get user consent, can we continue to show ads?_{quote}

Yes. Ads can still be shown, but *they cannot be personalised* without the relevant consent.

{quote}_What category would these consent and use cases fit in? Our current DMA/ePD does not have a toggle for personalised promotions and ads? When is this toggle specifically required?_{quote}

Our existing DMA/ePD setup does not include a dedicated toggle for _personalised promotions and ads_. At this stage, the existing *“targeting”* category can be used to capture this consent - but we will consider updating the categories.

{quote}_What does consent incrementally provide us? Is it the use case?_{quote}

Beyond legal compliance and having a valid lawful basis, collecting consent also makes commercial sense because the Transparency & Consent Framework (TCF). While TCF is not legally required, most major advertising partners only work with traffic that carries valid TCF consent signals.

----

I suggest we have a short call next week to discuss applicable requirements, your questions, and how we can approach this in Q1.

*Would you kindly set up the call during the time slots when I’m available?* Please also include anyone from your business side who should be involved.

