[~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] Hi! Please check my comments below.

# 

{quote}The partner set a period 1 business day for payment of funds after the reporting period{quote}

If I’m not mistaken, we don’t actually record the exact date when a partner payout is executed, right? In practice, we process partner payouts every Monday, meaning within 1 day after the end of the reporting period. A delay is only possible due to a technical issue on the bank’s side (which happened only 2–3 times during my 4 years here). To stay on the safe side, let’s indicate *2 days* for processing the payout. 

{quote}they set a reporting period to be not one calendar week, but the cycles of 7 consecutive days from the start of the month{quote}

I strongly recommend keeping our standard approach, which is *the calendar week.* The option proposed by the partner _does not match our payout cycle at all._

2.

{quote}Do we accept an obligation to provide a separate service acceptance act (clause 6)?{quote}

The Agent Report that we issue to all partners already serves as the service acceptance act, so issuing an additional act on top of it doesn’t make sense.

3.

{quote}Do we accept an obligation to provide a separate reconciliation act (clause 7)?{quote}

Yes, we can prepare a reconciliation act every month, but I suggest allowing *15 days* instead of 10 for its preparation.

