# *Break Right*


The lease is a fixed 12-month term with no ability for us to exit early. Can we request a tenant break option (e.g., after 3 or 6 months on one month’s notice). {color:#ff5630}This is not accepted. We are looking for a lease with no breaks.{color}

# *Repairing & Reinstatement Obligations (Clauses 3.1, 3.15.1-315.2)*


The lease requires full internal repair and decoration, reinstatement at end of term and payment of all landlord costs if we miss anything. For a small unmanned office,can we:

* add a Schedule of Condition;
* remove the redecoration obligation;
* limit reinstatement to alterations we actually make

{color:#ff5630}I have removed the redecoration obligations.{color}

# *Indemnity (Clause 3.14)*

There is a very broad, uncapped indemnity in favour of the landlord (covers all costs “directly or indirectly”). Can we narrow this to only losses caused directly by our negligence or breach. {color:#ff5630}Agreed. This has now been amended.{color}

# *Payment Terms (Clause 1.3.5)*

All charges must be paid within 7 days. Can we extend this to 14 days as the review and approval of invoices can take time to process. {color:#ff5630}Agreed and changed from 7 days to 14 Days. I have also amended Forfeiture Event (c){color}

# *Payment Method (Clause 3.1.1(a)(ii))*

The landlord can require payment by standing order. Can you please confirm if you are able accept payments through bank transfers. {color:#ff5630}Agreed. I have added in Bank Transfer at this clause 3.1.1(a)(ii){color}

# *Default Interest (Interest definition)*


Interest is 4% above NatWest base rate. Market is usually lower. Can we propose 2% above base. {color:#ff5630}Agreed – 2% - lease amended.{color}

# *Service Charge*

The service charge (£97) is uncapped and not itemised. Can we please request clarification and/or annual cap. {color:#ff5630}Agreed – I have added to the particulars  “The Service Charge payable by the Tenant must not exceed £1,500 per annum (exclusive of VAT), unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Tenant.”{color}

 

