Example:

* request A

{noformat}{
  "id": 7076414532114,
  "type": "support_case",
  "visibility": "internal",
  "localization": { "language": "en", "country_code": { "type": "global" } }
}
{noformat}

* request B (notice the difference in country code prop)

{noformat}{
  "id": 7076414532114,
  "type": "support_case",
  "visibility": "internal",
  "localization": { "countryCode": { "type": "global" }, "language": "en" }
}
{noformat}



I don’t know which response is rendered in the end but it it can be misleading if:

* response with countryCode in request is rendered AND
* user selects country different than Global
* on the backend we notice that country_code property is missing and we’ll fallback to Global since it’s optional
* global article is presented even if agent selected local variatn
